        "original_id": "8a606d7c-493b-5580-89aa-13982d57336d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul McCartney, John Lennon, Lennon–McCartney\n- Organizations: the Beatles\n- Products: \"She's a Woman\", \"I Feel Fine\"\n- Concepts: guitar feedback in popular music\n\nFacts:\n- In 1964, the Beatles released \"I Feel Fine\" as the A-side of their eighth British single.\n- In 1964, the Beatles released \"She's a Woman\" as the B-side to \"I Feel Fine\", their last single release of that year.\n- \"She's a Woman\" is a song by the Beatles that was written mainly by Paul McCartney and credited to Lennon–McCartney.\n- \"I Feel Fine\" is a song by the Beatles that was written by John Lennon and credited to Lennon–McCartney.\n- \"I Feel Fine\" features one of the first uses of guitar feedback in popular music.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d0634118-20e5-57c5-a8ba-e58302e640a7",
        "text": "Page: She's a Woman. Sentence: \"She's a Woman\" is a song by the Beatles, written mainly by Paul McCartney and credited to Lennon–McCartney.\nPage: She's a Woman. Sentence: It was released as the B-side to \"I Feel Fine\" in 1964, their last single release that year.\nPage: I Feel Fine. Sentence: \"I Feel Fine\" is a song written by John Lennon (credited to Lennon–McCartney) and released in 1964 by the Beatles as the A-side of their eighth British single.\nPage: I Feel Fine. Sentence: The song has one of the first uses of guitar feedback in popular music.",
